+## What a failed `beforeSession` guarantees
+
+A `beforeSession` that throws fails the turn through the same path as any other failure: the caller receives the rejection unchanged, `onError` is handed the session and the same thrown error it gets for any other orchestrator failure, and `afterSession` still runs ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L40)). `afterSession` therefore cannot tell a session that finished from one that never started, and what it may assume about a turn whose `beforeSession` threw is exactly this: no tool ran and the provider was never called, so there is nothing the turn allocated that still needs releasing ([validated by: error path calls onError then afterSession and never reaches the provider](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L566)). The durable record follows the same rule: `save` runs from the shared `finally` on this path as on any other, so a store that persists receives the session holding the user entry even though the turn never started, and [the session write signal spec](../hal-engine-session-write-signal/spec.md) owns that guarantee.
+
